# Code Review Checklist

Use this checklist when reviewing pull requests or agent-generated changes for EVOLVE.

## Clean Architecture

- [ ] Routes are thin — no business logic, no direct DB queries, no AI calls in `api/`
- [ ] Business logic lives in `services/`, not in routes or repositories
- [ ] Database access lives only in `repositories/`
- [ ] AI modules are invoked via services/orchestrator, never directly from routes
- [ ] One responsibility per class; no duplicated logic

## Security

- [ ] No hardcoded secrets, credentials, or API keys
- [ ] No plaintext passwords — only hashed values are stored, logged, or compared
- [ ] JWT secrets and tokens are never logged or returned in responses
- [ ] Input is validated via Pydantic schemas, not manually
- [ ] Response schemas never leak sensitive fields (password hashes, internal-only flags)

## Performance

- [ ] No obvious N+1 query patterns; relationship loading is intentional
- [ ] Indexes exist for columns used in filters, joins, and sort order
- [ ] No unbounded queries — list endpoints are paginated
- [ ] Sessions are managed via `get_db`, never opened/closed manually

## Database Review

- [ ] Models use SQLAlchemy 2.x `Mapped[]` / `mapped_column()` style
- [ ] Constraints (unique, check, foreign key) are explicit and named
- [ ] Enums store values, not Python member names, in PostgreSQL
- [ ] No raw SQL unless explicitly justified in the PR description

## Migration Review

- [ ] Exactly one migration per model change, included in the same PR
- [ ] `upgrade()` and `downgrade()` are both correct and reversible
- [ ] Autogenerated migrations were manually inspected, not blindly trusted
- [ ] Migration applied and verified against a real PostgreSQL instance before merge

## API Review

- [ ] Endpoints are versioned under `/api/v1/`
- [ ] Request/response schemas are separate Pydantic models, not raw ORM objects
- [ ] Error responses use consistent HTTP status codes and shapes
- [ ] Auth dependencies (`get_current_user`) are applied to protected routes

## Process

- [ ] PR is scoped to one concern, per `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md`
- [ ] `docs/ROADMAP.md` / `docs/TASKS.md` are updated when a sprint item completes
- [ ] `docs/DECISIONS.md` is updated for any new architecture or technology choice
